{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot","id":1268969,"title":"Am I the only one who wished M20 had more metaplot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-19T13:50:39-08:00","id":1268969,"title":"Am I the only one who wished M20 had more metaplot?","content":"I run Mage chronicles but enjoy reading about the other lines. Beckett's Jyhad Diary was a giant update of everything in Vampire that happened between 2004 and 2014 or so and is 500 gorgeous pages of notes, pictures, and such. I very much wish there were a Mage analog.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one that wished M20 had a metaplot update? The Metaplot asides gave options but didn't include much detail on &quot;hey, this is what a world where the avatar storm died down would look like&quot; or &quot;hey, here are some masters that could return to the other side of the gauntlet&quot;. I tend to get plots from picking elements from the metaplot and using those to create large arcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T14:15:47-08:00","id":1268981,"title":"","content":"WIth Only 3 books.. and a cookbook released I'd argue more of the metaplot has been set than 3 books into v20. V20 only really pulled ahead with the JHD.. Mage still has books in the line so it might get one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T16:57:55-08:00","id":1269024,"title":"","content":"The whole point of the X20 line is more retrospective more than progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T09:32:56-08:00","id":1269266,"title":"","content":"The thing with Mage is that there was never all that much metaplot to begin with and most of what was there only got bolted on with Revised to line it up with the \u201cEnd of Days\u201d from the other game lines.<br /> <br /> Once the \u201cEnd of Days\u201d got relegated to \u201cY2K-ish panic that didn\u2019t amount to anything\u201d the Mage metaplot basically collapsed into a heap of \u201cnot that important.\u201d Particularly since most of those metaplot elements were basically, this long-standing person/place/thing went BOOM! rather than something new being built.<br /> <br /> Old masters died, new masters rose to replace them, the rumors of XYZ\u2019s demise were greatly exaggerated. Life goes on for the newest generations of mages.<br /> <br /> Far more important from a Mage sense is how the various traditions and conventions have adapted to the last dozen or so years of innovations and now historical events and M20 has done a decent job of covering those.<br /> <br /> Mage is such a gonzo \u201cgo anywhere\u201d setting that I think trying to even maintain a metaplot would be a mistake. For the crew of the Etherjammer USS Challenger exploring the strange worlds and cultures of the Deep Umbra and the Hyde Park Cabal just trying to bring hope back to a blighted neighborhood the schemes of whomever is currently in charge of whichever faction just don\u2019t matter and, to the extent they do, are better served being tailored to that particular chronicle than made uniform across the game setting via a metaplot.<br /> <br /> Put more simply, I think Mage\u2019s metaplot works best if it\u2019s as subjective as the reality Mages manipulate is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T20:51:38-08:00","id":1269428,"title":"","content":"Chris24601 is wise.<br /> <br /> However, this advice might be extended to any of the lines and any of the metaplots. M20 does an admirable job of presenting a lot of options in terms of how the metaplot can be adapted, and kudos for that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T01:00:32-08:00","id":1269471,"title":"","content":"Personally I find the metaplot to be a pain, especially the sadly out-of-date 'apocalypse' meme they were running back in the day so I'm quite happy _not_ to have 'THE METAPLOT!' influencing any campaigns I want to run, it means there's not so much work to be done with persuading a well read player that things in this decade are not the same as things a decade or more ago.<br /> <br /> That sort of applies to this forum too - most forumites are very well read on different versions of the books and some like to state their canon views very firmly which kind of goes in opposition to the 20th anniversary's 'buffet' approach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T05:19:04-08:00","id":1269516,"title":"","content":"I do expect to see some Metaplot when Technocracy Reloaded comes out; in particular, I won't be a bit surprised if the Purge hinted at in one of the M20 boxes comes to pass in that book, and we get a restructured and refocused Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T05:46:35-08:00","id":1269522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1269266#post1269266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Mage is that there was never all that much metaplot to begin with and most of what was there only got bolted on with Revised to line it up with the \u201cEnd of Days\u201d from the other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. Most of the meta plot, such as it was, in 1st and 2nd edition was built around the fall of the House of Heklar (starting in Book of Chantries and creeping along into Horizon and then the Euthanatos tradition book), and the idea of newer, younger mages becoming leaders of the Traditions (Horizon, again). Beyond that, most of the metaplot was in the fiction novels, and if you were someone who didn't read them, all of this stuff got dumped on you when Tales of Magic: Dark Adventure and Digital Web 2.0 came out. After that was the Avatar Storm, which was a Year of Reckoning thing and first appeared in Masters of the Art. The only big change that <i>started</i> with the revised edition was what happened to several of the Crafts, IIRC, with all of the &quot;end of days&quot; stuff coming a few years later shortly after the Storytellers Handbook came out. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T07:59:30-08:00","id":1269566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1269516#post1269516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do expect to see some Metaplot when Technocracy Reloaded comes out; in particular, I won't be a bit surprised if the Purge hinted at in one of the M20 boxes comes to pass in that book, and we get a restructured and refocused Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hoping for the &quot;buffett&quot; approach Dogstar mentions, in that the book presents a number of opportunities. That would make it a more flexible tool for gamers, while a book with only one story is limited and too proscriptive. Maybe the Technocracy is riddled with a metastisized Nephandi threat, and maybe the Technos purged the Fallen, but both options should easily be available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T08:18:30-08:00","id":1269571,"title":"","content":"I probably should have started with an opener of why I like metaplot. This isn't complete nor is it categorical. If you throw it out the window and replace it with something you've created, awesome, but this is what I get from it. Every point has an alternative and one can say &quot;the storyteller should do that&quot;. Sure, but I'll never turn down help:<br /> <br /> *It provides something to direct the mood of the game. The sense of horror in Vampire is escalated by the existence of Gehenna cults and the belief that we're in the final nights. The mood of Dark Ages: Fae is anxiety about the world changing but the impending ending of the oath-truce greatly heightens this.<br /> <br /> *It gives the ST not just setting but direction. The WoD provides a setting but metaplot provides a sense of movement to that setting that makes the world seem alive and static.<br /> <br /> *It provides ideas. Giant events give you an idea of what can happen. There are scales at which the game does and doesn't make sense and metaplot can provide an upper limit.<br /> <br /> *It's fun. My characters have never visited the Digital Web or Doissetep but it's interesting to me to see what happened there.<br /> <br /> *it provides a way to address system problems. Mage's metaplot changes seemed to be heavily influenced by wanting to change the focus of the game to lower level players on this side of the gauntlet and the avatar storm, etc did a good job of that.<br /> <br /> So in that context, I find metaplot helpful. It gives me cues on how to play the game at a level I may vaguely feel but that the writers and developers maybe have put their finger on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T02:25:55-08:00","id":1269774,"title":"","content":"I really like Mage's metaplot actually, it's easier to follow than the one in Vampire and it doesn't have the same problems that one had (a bunch of canon NPCs doing everything and a lot of conflicting info).<br /> <br /> Also it more or less presented a story to give you ideas to use. The very big game changer was the Avatar Storm and the Union &quot;winning&quot;, but even that whole &quot;we now want to go low key street based&quot; lasted like 3 or 4 books until Revised started giving lots of options to circumvent the Avatar Storm and the Sphinx basically reignited the Ascension War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 11-22-2018, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T12:10:47-08:00","id":1270657,"title":"","content":"I think that the Technocracy's stance in regard to Mystic Mages should be more defined and consistent throughout the Technocracy in the future, as a metaplot development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1269516#post1269516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do expect to see some Metaplot when Technocracy Reloaded comes out; in particular, I won't be a bit surprised if the Purge hinted at in one of the M20 boxes comes to pass in that book, and we get a restructured and refocused Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot; Book of the Fallen &quot; could also have some metaplot developments or options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-25-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T15:01:27-08:00","id":1270699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270657#post1270657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Technocracy's stance in regard to Mystic Mages should be more defined and consistent throughout the Technocracy in the future, as a metaplot development.</div> </div> </div> </div>For various reasons, I just went back to where their attitudes follow the traditional real world technocrat ones of &quot;We know what's best for you, peasant, so shut up&quot;, with the only real variation being if the punishment for not shutting up is reeducation or liquidation. Members of the Union who decide this is wrong have to defect to the Traditions or go on the run as Orphans. Ironically, I used to be one of the most vocal advocates for making the Technocracy playable protagonists with a valid and possibly heroic world view. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T07:03:44-08:00","id":1270820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270699#post1270699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For various reasons, I just went back to where their attitudes follow the traditional real world technocrat ones of &quot;We know what's best for you, peasant, so shut up&quot;, with the only real variation being if the punishment for not shutting up is reeducation or liquidation. Members of the Union who decide this is wrong have to defect to the Traditions or go on the run as Orphans. Ironically, I used to be one of the most vocal advocates for making the Technocracy playable protagonists with a valid and possibly heroic world view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you change from a possibly heroic Technocracy all the way to a merciless and dogmatic Technocracy ?<br /> One of the reasons why the extremely ruthless Technocracy doesn't work for me is that such a portrayal doesn't go in line with the Technocracy's mission statement of exploring and investigating reality. If Mystic Mages are capable of the feats that they are, doesn't this merit investigation, and respect ? Also, I think that it might very well be that the objectives which involve guiding and influencing mundane humans can be accomplished more easily by Technocrats if cooperation with Mystic Mages is undertaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T07:29:45-08:00","id":1270826,"title":"","content":"It is important to remember this is the World of Darkness we are discussing. There are no heroes here, with the possible exception of the PCs themselves. Further, there are no &quot;good&quot; institutions, and that includes the Conventions of the Technocracy (and the Traditions as well). They are all hopelessly compromised. Also, there is a difference between a recruiting line like &quot;...mission statement of exploring and investigating reality,&quot; and the actual working principal, which is more <i>Harrison Bergeron</i> than <i>Star Trek</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T11:26:51-08:00","id":1270886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270820#post1270820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you change from a possibly heroic Technocracy all the way to a merciless and dogmatic Technocracy ?<br /> One of the reasons why the extremely ruthless Technocracy doesn't work for me is that such a portrayal doesn't go in line with the Technocracy's mission statement of exploring and investigating reality. If Mystic Mages are capable of the feats that they are, doesn't this merit investigation, and respect ? Also, I think that it might very well be that the objectives which involve guiding and influencing mundane humans can be accomplished more easily by Technocrats if cooperation with Mystic Mages is undertaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy actually has a Mission statement and its not &quot;Exploring and investigating reality&quot; <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bring <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Stasis\" target=\"_blank\">Stasis</a> and order to the Universe. Predictability brings safety. Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be won.</li> <li>Convince the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Masses\" target=\"_blank\">Masses</a> from the benevolence of science, commerce, politics, and of the power of Rationality. Conflict and suffering will be eliminated in our Utopia.</li> <li>Preserve the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gauntlet_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Gauntlet</a> and the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Horizon_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Horizon</a>. Chaotic individuals who open gateways with impunity threaten the stability of our world. Uncontrolled portals also allow outside forces, such as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephandi\" target=\"_blank\">Nephandi</a>, access to our world. This must never happen.</li> <li>Define the nature of the universe. Knowledge must be absolute or chaos will envelop all. The elemental forces of the universe must not be left to the caprices of the unknown.</li> <li>Destroy <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Reality_Deviants\" target=\"_blank\">Reality Deviants</a>. Their recklessness threatens our security and our progress toward Unity.</li> <li>Shepherd the Masses; protect them from themselves and others.</li> </ol><br /> Its right there.. its in the guide to the Technocracy, its in mage 20.. there's no place where the Technocracy is guided by &quot;Explore and investigate reality&quot; vs &quot;Create orderly Utopia&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T11:38:40-08:00","id":1270892,"title":"","content":"Indeed, the idea of knowledge it's always subordinate to the idea of defining an orderly reality with the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Every and each mention of something akin to investigation within the Technocracy it's always envelopped by the idea of Control. They may invest resources to discover what makes Deviants tick, but that's strictly in order of eradicating them. As it's clearly stated in their Mission Statement, that we can read in Lian's post.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't mean that they don't care about investigation or exploration, but merely than these are secondary goals instrumental to their actual mission. As an example, let's analize the fourth:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">4. <b>Define the nature of the universe</b>. Knowledge must be absolute <u>or chaos will envelop all</u>. The elemental forces of <u>the universe must not be left to the caprices of the unknown</u>.</span> </div> </div> </div>To &quot;define&quot; something it's not the same as to discover or investigate it.<br /> <br /> Then they say, Knowledge must be absolute. But that's to prevent chaos from enveloping all. Again, knowledge here seems to be subordinate to the idea of order.<br /> <br /> And what does imply to science the idea of preventing &quot;the caprices of the unknown&quot;: In real science one studies the unknown and if our definitions don't accomodate reality we change the definitions. This mission statement doesn't sound like that, what it says it's that the unknown shouldn't be allowed to have power (over the forces of the universe). A rather odd argument for a scientist: Usually the unknown isn't something to be feared.<br /> <br /> It rather sounds to me like it's more important to prevent the unknown to interfere with the statical model of the universe (our definitions that allow absolute knowledge) than to discover new stuff that could challenge such definitions. The goal of discovering stuff it's subordinate to a &quot;model&quot; that's pre-defined (the fabled Technocratic Paradigm), and the stuff that doesn't accomodate to that model has to be eradicated, as latter shown in the Principle that comes just after it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">5. Destroy <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Reality_Deviants\" target=\"_blank\">Reality Deviants</a>. Their recklessness threatens our security and our progress toward Unity.</span> </div> </div> </div>It trully can't be clearer than that.<br /> <br /> Or that's how I interpret all of this. Surely other interpretations are possible.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, <i>the fact that in each an every principle the idea of knowledge appears tied to the idea of averting chaos or fostering stasis really shouldn't be ignored in any interpretation</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-26-2018, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T15:09:34-08:00","id":1270942,"title":"","content":"A lot of what it seems some of the people who want a kinder gentler Technocracy basically describes is... the Society of Ether. This is not to say that the Technocracy is intrinsically Evil or they can't be reasoned with on the local level. Even Control can mandate which Reality Deviants should be prioritized. But the Technocracy's Goal is a world without Monsters. A world without Darkness. That is it first and foremost. They are Hard Men Making Hard Choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T15:09:34-08:00","id":1270943,"title":"","content":"As I said, I went back to the idea that they share the same ideals and drives as real world technocrats of the 20th century. The sort of people Orwell, Huxley and Bradbury were writing about in 1984, Brave New World, and Fahrenheit 451, and the sort of real world people who were advocating things like eugenics, the New Soviet Man, and rule by unelected &quot;enlightened&quot; elites. Science, technology and academia are all just means to an end: Control. <br /> <br /> (For this reason, in my games, the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts have never been part of the Union, instead being founded on the ideas of the wonder of scientific discovery, and of intellectual freedom, respectively, largely in defiance of the Union's ideas. However, I do, on occasion, run a Technocracy game as a heroic pulp sci fi thing. Just because I can and I feel like it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T16:29:39-08:00","id":1270970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270820#post1270820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you change from a possibly heroic Technocracy all the way to a merciless and dogmatic Technocracy ?<br /> One of the reasons why the extremely ruthless Technocracy doesn't work for me is that such a portrayal doesn't go in line with the Technocracy's mission statement of exploring and investigating reality. If Mystic Mages are capable of the feats that they are, doesn't this merit investigation, and respect ? Also, I think that it might very well be that the objectives which involve guiding and influencing mundane humans can be accomplished more easily by Technocrats if cooperation with Mystic Mages is undertaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry? The Technocracy doesn't <i>have</i> a mission statement of exploring and investigating reality. The precepts of Damian are the closest thing to a Technocratic Mission Statement, and they're all about redefining a chaotic reality as something predictable, and walling off the pieces the Technocracy doesn't like past the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Precept 1.) &quot;Bring Stasis and Order to the universe. Predictability brings safety.once all is discovered and all is known unity will be won.<br /> <br /> Precept one is the closest the precepts get to a mission statement of exploring and investigating reality. However it's not a mission statement so much as a statement of the Unions <i>win condition.</i> And that condition is when all is discovered and all is known. When there is no mystery and no room for chaos in their perfect new order.<br /> <br /> Precept 2.) &quot;Convince the masses of the benevolence of science, commerce, and politics. Conflict and Suffering will be eliminated in our utopia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Included this largely because I felt like including all the precepts, but the wording here is clearly construction focused, rather than investigation focused. Their goal is not to investigate and make available the fruits of that investigation, but to convince the masses of the benevolence of their brand of magic by way of good works.<br /> <br /> Precept 3.) &quot;Preserve the Gauntlet and the Horizon. Chaotic Individuals who open gateways with impunity threaten the stability of our world. Uncontrolled portals also allow outside forces, such as the Nephandi, access to our world. This must never happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, largely included because I wanted to include all of them. But this demonstrates the incompatibility of the Umbra, in which anything is possible and as a realm of chaos, with the perfect order the Union aspires to create.<br /> <br /> Precept 4.) &quot;Define the nature of the universe. Knowledge must be absolute or chaos will envelop all. The elemental forces of the universe must not be left to the Caprices of the Unknown.&quot;<br /> <br /> And here we get to the brunt of it. The laws of the universe must be defined, and created whole cloth by the union, because the building blocks of their world cannot be left to the 'caprices of the unknown' They can't simply make do with what they discover to be the laws. They must break down the world that was there before and rebuild it to their liking. This is the primary conflict with the Sons of Ether, who are totally willing to apply the scientific method to a universe that makes no sense and accept the answer it gives back, maddening and contradictory as those answers will be. The union however, demands order. And if the world won't provide it, then they will kill the world and build order atop it's corpse.<br /> <br /> Precept 5.) &quot;Destroy Reality Deviants. Their recklessness threatens our security and our progress towards unity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Precept 6.) &quot;Shepherd the masses. Protect them from themselves and others.&quot;<br /> <br /> These last two are fairly self explanatory. However the term 'reality deviant' is telling. They don't deny that mystic mages have power. The issue is the source of that power and the means by which they use it. Magic is chaos. It's potential is infinite and varied. Though they make use of Magic, the Union's ultimate goal is a world without it. A world where the laws are redefined to eliminate magic and any need for magic.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And it seems several people beat me to the punch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T00:40:35-08:00","id":1271064,"title":"","content":"I'll just add that the Void Engineers are the closest thing the Technocracy has to \u201cexplore and investigate reality\u201d; and even they're more about taming the wild and pushing back the chaos than they are about exploring and investigating. That said, I could see Navalon taking a different approach once it separates from the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T08:14:37-08:00","id":1271144,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget what the technocracy is not even when taking account of the retconning of their intentions with the guide of the technocracy.<br /> <br /> 1/ They are not, never were and at this rate won't live long enough to ever be scientists.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;the technocracy is about reason and science&quot; is pure propaganda. Scientists don't try to eliminate things that don't conform to their models, scientists don't arbitrarily decides that some things are &quot;deviants&quot; from the way things should be. Scientists don't deny obvious phenomenom as real in order to never change it's worldview.<br /> <br /> That goes for the Void Engineers as well, despite their more relaxed views of the universe, they are still pushing an agenda, classifying discoveries between the &quot;allowed to stay in the universe&quot; and &quot;deviant phenomena&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a world where supernatural events are common, reason isn't that magic don't exist, in fact, even the order of reason was misnamed.<br /> <br /> The only real group of enlightened scientists amongs the awakened are the Sons of Ether, even though they have the habit of drowning simple supernatural phenomenom under unecessary scientobabble.<br /> <br /> It's truly visible when confronting the two organisations's philosophies:<br /> <br /> Technocratic Union : We will make reality conform our vision.<br /> <br /> Sons of Ether : Like the metaphor of Troy in the book of ether, when facing unknown phenomenom, we will extend our theories of reality to take account of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2/ They're not Hard Men making Hard Choices<br /> <br /> They are men making Stupid Choices.<br /> <br /> The technocracy would do a better job to create a world without darkness if they did not outright denied the umbra as an important thing in reality.<br /> <br /> If they would have given the umbra the study it deserved as scientists, they would have seen that the umbra isn't just full of aliens ready to invade , but also full of aliens ready to help them.<br /> <br /> Was it so hard to seek spirits of Order, of Protecting the innocent, of Hope for a Safer Future?<br /> <br /> They also don't understand, due to considering the Umbra as &quot;the other&quot;, the symbiotic relationship between both worlds and the use they could get with it, that sending missions in the middle umbra to kill banes could make life in cities better, by sending necronauts, or allying with wraiths, they could spy the supernaturals of the whole world beyond the veils, seeking the Ideal perfect society, etc...<br /> <br /> <br /> 3/ Rather than exterminating anything that don't conform to their ideals, they could have made allies with sympathising supernaturals<br /> <br /> <br /> 4/ Finally, by accepting others's insights, they might be able to ask themselves if their ideals is actually good, or if the means are actually necessary.<br /> <br /> It make me laugh to hear the common defense of &quot;the technocracy offer medicine, electricity and no monster in the dark&quot;.<br /> <br /> But seriously, all traditions can offer at least the same ammount of good to humanity, if not more, and all the setbacks of the magical reality also exist in the world the technocracy want to create.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T11:39:57-08:00","id":1271197,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271144#post1271144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2/ They're not Hard Men making Hard Choices<br /> <br /> They are men making Stupid Choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little misguided. You need to take in count that IOC characters don't know what the readers know, and that the Technocracy it's a large institution that's quite corrup but still has a lot of people who believes in their Principles.<br /> <br /> Technocrats are human supremacists. The goal of the OoR was to put humans in a pedestal, and it can be argued that whitin the limited understanding of reality that they have (an understanding that comes from their origins as a small cabal of the Order of Hermes) they did just that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The technocracy would do a better job to create a world without darkness if they did not outright denied the umbra as an important thing in reality.<br /> <br /> If they would have given the umbra the study it deserved as scientists, they would have seen that the umbra isn't just full of aliens ready to invade , but also full of aliens ready to help them.<br /> <br /> Was it so hard to seek spirits of Order, of Protecting the innocent, of Hope for a Safer Future? </div> </div> </div>Technocrats are wrong at relegating DimSci and Cosmology to a single Convention. To be blind to spirit was a choice born of Hubris that impairs their capability to react to certain threats. However, they have good reasons to think the Umbra isn't important (or, rather, not in the ways you mention), and not all of them are wrong.<br /> <br /> Technocracy it's founded upon the premise that the Consensus controls/it's Reality.<br /> <br /> Their goals and what they do can't be understood without this premise. And as far as Mage it's concerned they could be right (Mage Methapisics do assume that the Consensus it's, if not absolute, at least a fundamental force that shapes Reality)<br /> <br /> Because the Consensus shapes Reality, asking the spirit of Order it's only marginaly better than to make a pool: The spirit of Order it's the concept of Order, that's defined by what humans consider Orderly, and not the other way arround. If OoR had asked the spirit of Order what Order it's in the dark ages, it would have answered with the Divine Order/Monarchy and other stuff that really don't place humans in a pedestal.<br /> <br /> Since the goal was to place humans in a pedestal, asking the spirits in a world where Order, Protection and Hope aren't about that won't do. The OoR set themselves to Change what those Concepts mean. In doing that the spirits would change too<br /> <br /> Mages change Reality. Spirits are manifestations of Reality, and thus also are to be changed (new concepts create and empower new spirits, while old spirits based on less popular concepts get weaker). If you don't operate on Werewolf cosmology nor assume a &quot;Dreamspeakers are Right&quot; mentality, this shouldn't be so hard to accept.<br /> <br /> This makes even more sense when one considers that Technocracy descends from the Order of Hermes. In their view, Humans have a greater methaphisical potential than Spirits do, they just have to realize this potential. Spirits are useful to study and to employ, but ultimately the Enligthened knows best and what they want Hope to be it's more important than what Hope is.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying that Technocrats ARE Right(tm) about how Reality works, I'm just implying that they could be and have few reasons to suspect they aren't (I'm of the opinion that Mage doesn't take a definite stance about who is right. And to the exent that mage takes a definite stance about anything, the Consensus = Reality seems to come on top).<br /> <br /> And if they're right, then the Umbra isn't *that* important (not in that way). Spirits don't know better than Mages do. (of course, they could be wrong, but if they are it's not because they're stupid, but merely because their understanding has limits)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also don't understand, due to considering the Umbra as &quot;the other&quot;, the symbiotic relationship between both worlds and the use they could get with it, that sending missions in the middle umbra to kill banes could make life in cities better, by sending necronauts, or allying with wraiths, they could spy the supernaturals of the whole world beyond the veils, seeking the Ideal perfect society, etc... </div> </div> </div>Banes are remarkably less important in Mage than they are in Werewolf. Because the relationship between the Umbra and Earth is more asimetrical in Mage than in Werewolf, you can't kill Banes if you don't make the life in cities better to begin with.<br /> In Mage it's rather hard to kill spirits permanently (w/o Spheres at 5), while in Werewolf it's merely a matter of going to the other side and slashing them to death. This is because spirits are backed by the Consensus, and thus would just reform unless the concept/fact they represent ceases to exist or weakens a lot. A mechanical difference that speaks volumes about what each game focuses into. In Mage, Banes are a symptom rather than the sickness.<br /> <br /> Allying with wraiths it's simply not possible. It would be akin to &quot;ally with Humanity&quot;. For instance: You can try to ally with Stigia, but that would imply being enemy to the other Dark Kingdoms, Rebels, Heretics, and other factions of Wraiths.<br /> More so, even allying with one faction of Wraiths wouldn't be possible because Wraith factions either have a policy against humans that meddle with the afterlife, have goals that more or less oppose the Technocracy or are too disorganized. Combine that with the lack of knowledge Techncoracy has on the worlds (and thus the politics) at the other side of the Veil (necronauts are rare) and you see why this just isn't an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3/ Rather than exterminating anything that don't conform to their ideals, they could have made allies with sympathising supernaturals </div> </div> </div>Technocrats do ally with other supernaturals from time to time, but when you have a human supremacist agenda it's hard to make long standing allies among non humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4/ Finally, by accepting others's insights, they might be able to ask themselves if their ideals is actually good, or if the means are actually necessary. </div> </div> </div>XDXD<br /> <br /> Perish the thought! Mages are never wrong about anything! And if Reality says otherwise then Reality it's Wrong.<br /> <br /> Now, really, the Technocracy it's stupid in this sense. But so are all mages. It's the theme of Hubris. If mages were able to sit down and solve their differences, admiting that they may be wrong, then there would have been no Ascencion War.<br /> <br /> If we go to that, if humans were able to sit down and solve our differences there would be no wars, no nuclear arsenals, no hunger in the world...so we aren't much better, really!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It make me laugh to hear the common defense of &quot;the technocracy offer medicine, electricity and no monster in the dark&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This defense is wrong...to an extent. I myself have argued a lot against those who believe that the Technocracy it's about science and those who believe WoD got out of the Dark Ages just because of them, but I think you're going to the other extreme which isn't right either.<br /> <br /> There are monsters in the dark, alright, but these monsters are afraid to reveal themselves to the public. The Technocracy boasts that they vanquished the dragons and other blatant mosters (and certainly Bigones seem to respond to the Consensus), and that forced the rest into hidding. To what extent this boast it's true depends on the ST, but the Technocracy had it's hand in the Inquisition and the killing of magical creatures (most of which were dangerous).<br /> <br /> The Technocracy helped medicine, electricity, etc, to grow. While one, again, can't demonstrate to what extent their influence was fundamental for the rise of the industrial age it's irrefutable that they had it's hand in it. The ST Handbook (Revised edition) goes so far as to say, out of character, that every innovation comes from Mages (the Technocracy in particular) while normal humans mostly build and polish the product.<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But seriously, all traditions can offer at least the same ammount of good to humanity, if not more, and all the setbacks of the magical reality also exist in the world the technocracy want to create. </div> </div> </div>They can, but they didn't and they mostly won't. That's the problem of the Traditions: They're more elitist than the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> For the Traditions magick it's something you have to either earn trough grueling training or have imposed on you (Chosen One style) in order to employ it. The attempts of the Traditions of sharing their Tools with the masses it's a recent development, and even now they are more about encouraging &quot;spiritual growth&quot; than about giving the golden keys to the power.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the true good guys of Mage were the Craftmasons. They were the ones that put normal humans above even mages and saw fit to share their instruments with the masses. Technocrats fell from this lofty ideal, they wanted their privileges and killed the Craftmasons to keep Control...but still, in spite of mages being all too human, the Order managed to provide a lot of good to humanity at large.<br /> <br /> The now called Traditions wouldn't have done this by themselves, their Paradigm was (and still IS) against providing power to the unenligthened. And thus it's reasonable to think that human development would have, at least, suffered a setback without the OoR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-27-2018, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T14:58:43-08:00","id":1271268,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the Syndicate still does put the Masses at least on a par with the Enlightened, albeit for selfish reasons (the more options Sleepers have to work with, the more Primal Ventures can be founded, and the richer the Syndicate becomes as it funds them and harvests Quintessence from them). <br /> <br /> But yeah; lets not fall into the fallacy of the excluded middle: just because the most extreme arguments in Dave of the Technocracy have flaws, that doesn't mean that the opposite is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T15:34:44-08:00","id":1271289,"title":"","content":"&quot;That's a little misguided. You need to take in count that IOC characters don't know what the readers know, and that the Technocracy it's a large institution that's quite corrup but still has a lot of people who believes in their Principles.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do take account of it. Based on guide to the technocracy, the revised convention books and the order of reason guide, the technocracy knows all the point I make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Technocrats are wrong at relegating DimSci and Cosmology to a single Convention. To be blind to spirit was a choice born of Hubris that impairs their capability to react to certain threats. However, they have good reasons to think the Umbra isn't important (or, rather, not in the ways you mention), and not all of them are wrong.<br /> <br /> Technocracy it's founded upon the premise that the Consensus controls/it's Reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, it's more &quot;the Consensus SHOULD control it's reality&quot;. Otherwise, the Void Engineers wouldn't spend so much efforts to patrol the gauntlet and the horizon, they are countless spirits that, outside of mage's influence, tries to and succeed in going through or interfering with people's lives beyond the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Since the goal was to place humans in a pedestal, asking the spirits in a world where Order, Protection and Hope aren't about that won't do. The OoR set themselves to Change what those Concepts mean. In doing that the spirits would change too<br /> <br /> Mages change Reality. Spirits are manifestations of Reality, and thus also are to be changed (new concepts create and empower new spirits, while old spirits based on less popular concepts get weaker). If you don't operate on Werewolf cosmology nor assume a &quot;Dreamspeakers are Right&quot; mentality, this shouldn't be so hard to accept.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Changed by humanity don't make spirits unimportant or strategically devoid of interests.<br /> <br /> Umbrood do try to manipulate humankind to highten their importance and powers, incarnations of ideas fight over each others and impact the sleeping world.<br /> <br /> And as every ideas exist in the high umbra, an intelligent technocracy would ally with, say, the &quot;Order is all that protect the masses&quot; spirits and help them undermine the &quot;Order is what decide the Almighty&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This makes even more sense when one considers that Technocracy descends from the Order of Hermes. In their view, Humans have a greater methaphisical potential than Spirits do, they just have to realize this potential. Spirits are useful to study and to employ, but ultimately the Enligthened knows best and what they want Hope to be it's more important than what Hope is.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The order of hermes wouldn't dare to say that in front of a high umbrood court, or facing an Incarna. They also depend on bargain with angels quite a lot.<br /> <br /> The OOH desires to become superior to umbrood, but there's a difference between believing you have a potential and demonstrating it.<br /> <br /> It's not so much about whenever spirits are more powerful or know better than humans, it's that they are at worse a great ressource, at best great allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Allying with wraiths it's simply not possible. It would be akin to &quot;ally with Humanity&quot;. For instance: You can try to ally with Stigia, but that would imply being enemy to the other Dark Kingdoms, Rebels, Heretics, and other factions of Wraiths.&quot;<br /> <br /> The technocracy do have a hell lot of inside agents in humanity. Both knowing and unknowing to it's goals. There's nothing stopping the technocracy from doing the same with wraiths, like the giovanni does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;More so, even allying with one faction of Wraiths wouldn't be possible because Wraith factions either have a policy against humans that meddle with the afterlife, have goals that more or less oppose the Technocracy or are too disorganized. Combine that with the lack of knowledge Techncoracy has on the worlds (and thus the politics) at the other side of the Veil (necronauts are rare) and you see why this just isn't an option.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not allying with Wraiths the 'race&quot;, it's allying with wraiths the individuals, especially malcontent wraiths, or wraiths that were members of the technocracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;If we go to that, if humans were able to sit down and solve our differences there would be no wars, no nuclear arsenals, no hunger in the world...so we aren't much better, really!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not solving differences, it's analysing the way you're doing things based on the evidence you have.<br /> <br /> The technocracy use things (like the horizon) that they deem to never be in the hands of the masses. And they know a lot about the umbra possibilities. There's no way, after all the babble about how strategically advanced the NWO and the rest of the technocracy is said to be, that they never even though about using sympathetic spirits for their cause.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;There are monsters in the dark, alright, but these monsters are afraid to reveal themselves to the public.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of them aren't, okay, it's the whole point of the Masquerade, but the Garous aren't afraid of humanity, they're staying in the dark due to a millenia old rule, demons have yet to do anything as they're just coming back from hell, and they are hint in the Bygone Bestiary that quite messy creatures, who aren't afraid of the consensus, are coming out of their sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;They can, but they didn't and they mostly won't. That's the problem of the Traditions: They're more elitist than the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> For the Traditions magick it's something you have to either earn trough grueling training or have imposed on you (Chosen One style) in order to employ it. The attempts of the Traditions of sharing their Tools with the masses it's a recent development, and even now they are more about encouraging &quot;spiritual growth&quot; than about giving the golden keys to the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not about magick, it's about magic.<br /> <br /> It's not about people mass awakening, it's about people accepting magical reality in order to massively be able to use linear magic.<br /> <br /> Take genetic manipulation, once it was only possible by progenitors enlightened science, now, it's so much ingrained into the consensus that anyone with a lab can attempt it.<br /> <br /> Same thing with magic without a k. If the traditions have their ways, the message that will spread in the world would be &quot;you all have the spark of magic in you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not enough to trigger mass awakening perhaps, but enough to create a new consensual reality where magical things happens everyday.<br /> <br /> <br /> In our real world, people believe they have healing abilities.<br /> <br /> In a world of darkness where the tradition winned, it would be reality. What illness would exist when any ten person have &quot;the gift&quot; and can heal all issues?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And let's be honest Aleph, the whole &quot;the tradition never tried to disseminate it's tools in the consensus&quot; is just a narrative excuse to explain why the setting is the modern day world and not a high fantasy setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like the revised edition &quot;traditions influence in the masses is more spiritual growth&quot; is just an excuse to avoid seeing a major shift in the world that would lead to mass numbers of sorcerers, and the end of mage's main narrative.<br /> <br /> That's the same reason why the Garou will always fail to gain significant victory over the Wyrm, it would break the game narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Take homeopathy and the lot of &quot;alternative medicine&quot;.<br /> <br /> Their mass popularity in the WOD is a good thing, after all, if anyone believe you can cure cancer with essential oil, it will become so.<br /> <br /> In fact, it should already be so with the common belief in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As Phil Brucado explain in the M20 book of secrets, most people believe in magic, in a form and another, and believe they can do it, be it through prayer of seeing the local medicine man or joining a wicca circle.<br /> <br /> If the modern wod is anything like the real life modern world, then the traditions have won. And the consensus would have shifted to match this new reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The now called Traditions wouldn't have done this by themselves, their Paradigm was (and still IS) against providing power to the unenligthened. And thus it's reasonable to think that human development would have, at least, suffered a setback without the OoR.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The order of hermes is all for the development of humanity, the only difference with the order of reason was that the hermetic though the first thing to do was to understand magick before using it.<br /> <br /> I know the ars magica is no longuer related to the wod, but it develop quite well early industrialition with the help of hermetic magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T17:57:56-08:00","id":1271348,"title":"","content":"I'll have a more in-depth response later; but for now, I'll just note that you're right that Ars Magica isn't related to WoD anymore. DAMage gives a better picture of the early Hermetics; and according to it, the Hermetics who promoted early industrialization were (wait for it\u2026) the Craftmasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T09:56:12-08:00","id":1271479,"title":"","content":"No. The Technocracy believes that the consensus DOES control reality. The Void engineers patrol the umbra because their goal is to expand reality.<br /> <br /> Also, you're talking about a group who insists on rebuilding every members mind from the ground up as a basic part of joining that everyone goes through to purge mental contaminants.<br /> <br /> And you seriously think they're going to be too eager to work with any old random spirit who says hi? No. They won't. However they do in fact work with spirits, pattern spiders in particular are called out several times.<br /> <br /> Also, no, the consensus doesn't work like that. Unconscious belief only has so much force behind it. If you split belief between modern medicine and Homeopathy, you don't get equally viable magical medicine and modern medicine that can cure everything. You get weaker and weaker versions of both. This is why the progenitors will kill you for being a faith healer even in othertimes cold conflict zones. Because you're weakening modern medicine with every convert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T12:21:19-08:00","id":1271532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271479#post1271479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you're talking about a group who insists on rebuilding every members mind from the ground up as a basic part of joining that everyone goes through to purge mental contaminants.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are quite the purists indeed. However that's also criticeable. Conditioning it's the force behind the inhability of Technocrats to react to Treath Null, and Void Engineers (the ones that will ally with friendly EDE's) are known to break their Conditioning (and place some of their own, that's much less restrictive).<br /> <br /> One could argue that Conditioning has it's place. It's advantageous in the sense that it prevents the Traditions from infiltrating them, counters certain forms of mind control and prevents normal insanity. More impirtantly, it allows everyone (including mortals) to follow the same broad Paradigm that allows to share Wonders, which it's the main strenght of the Technocracy. But it's still rather heavy handed (and criticized within the very Union, altrough not when NWO it's listening).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it's more &quot;the Consensus SHOULD control it's reality&quot;. Otherwise, the Void Engineers wouldn't spend so much efforts to patrol the gauntlet and the horizon, they are countless spirits that, outside of mage's influence, tries to and succeed in going through or interfering with people's lives beyond the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Enginseer-42 says, they believe that Consensus controls Reality. Technocrats don't believe Umbrood are outside the influence of the Consensus, but the Consensus isn't <i>wise</i> - the Consensus needs to be controled. That's what Technocrats do. They believe their efforts strengthen the Gauntlet and help making these incursions from Spirits a non threat. If spirits, even good intended ones, were allowed to interact with humans, human belief would weaken the Gauntlet and then evil spirits would have an easier time entering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changed by humanity don't make spirits unimportant or strategically devoid of interests.<br /> <br /> Umbrood do try to manipulate humankind to highten their importance and powers, incarnations of ideas fight over each others and impact the sleeping world </div> </div> </div>Of course they can be a resource, but what I intended to higlight was that they're not <i>essential </i>to the long term plans of the Technocracy as far as they understand Reality.<br /> <br /> While the Traditions were talking with spirits and asking for their aid, the Technocrats were talking with humans and changing their minds. And - lo and behold - the sect that chosed to not seek the aid of spirits it's the one that's on top of Mage business. Why would they change their mind about that particular policy?. Perhaps they should, but you can't blame them for being blind to this particular weakness.<br /> <br /> That being said, as was mentioned Technocrats do ally with certain spirits. It's just that they don't do this as much as the Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as every ideas exist in the high umbra, an intelligent technocracy would ally with, say, the &quot;Order is all that protect the masses&quot; spirits and help them undermine the &quot;Order is what decide the Almighty&quot;.<br /> <br /> The order of hermes wouldn't dare to say that in front of a high umbrood court, or facing an Incarna. They also depend on bargain with angels quite a lot.<br /> <br /> The OOH desires to become superior to umbrood, but there's a difference between believing you have a potential and demonstrating it.<br /> <br /> It's not so much about whenever spirits are more powerful or know better than humans, it's that they are at worse a great ressource, at best great allies. </div> </div> </div>Technocracy has presence in the Umbra, they hold charges within the Cyberrealm (which the Traditions call dystopia) and occasionally ally with the Spiders. If we take in count ToJ:Ascencion &quot;almost canon&quot; scenario, the White Tower (the main Realm of the Technocracy, whose real location it's left as a mystery in the canon) exists whitin the Realm that represents Goverment and Authority in the Astral Umbra.<br /> <br /> A spirit of &quot;Order is all that protect the masses&quot; it's never mentioned to exist in the canon, yet you infer it exists. Then why not infer too that the technocracy IT'S allied with such a spirit even if they don't mention it? I would imagine that they're allied with a lot of spirits akin to the one you mention. It's just that they won't care as much about such alliances as they care about controling real world goverments because they see these spirits as a reflection of those.<br /> <br /> Technocrats have presence in the Umbra, but they ultimately do not wish spirits to control human affairs. Still they have the Familiar background (with an &quot;appropriate name&quot;, of course), and as any one with DimSci 1 (not rare even outside the VE) can attest, these are EDE's. So, at least as a resource Technocrats do ally with spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The technocracy do have a hell lot of inside agents in humanity. Both knowing and unknowing to it's goals. There's nothing stopping the technocracy from doing the same with wraiths, like the giovanni does. </div> </div> </div>The thing that stops Technocrats from doing the same it's that human agents are easy to come by and are dupes that don't know who they're working for. Necronauts are rare, and Wraiths have a Shadow (aren't trustworthy) and are very aware of the supernatural (aren't dupes). There's no way for the Techncoracy to treat a Necropolis the same way they treat a normal city. Especially not with the little understanding they have on the Dark Umbra and it's politics (which it's hard to overcme because necronauts are rare).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not allying with Wraiths the 'race&quot;, it's allying with wraiths the individuals, especially malcontent wraiths, or wraiths that were members of the technocracy. </div> </div> </div>Again, there's not a single Wraith in the canon who's an ex member of the Technocracy. Yet you infer it exists. Why not infer too that the Techncoracy can be allied with such an ex-member?. Necronauts certainly could use the help of an insider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not about magick, it's about magic.<br /> <br /> It's not about people mass awakening, it's about people accepting magical reality in order to massively be able to use linear magic.<br /> <br /> Same thing with magic without a k. If the traditions have their ways, the message that will spread in the world would be &quot;you all have the spark of magic in you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not enough to trigger mass awakening perhaps, but enough to create a new consensual reality where magical things happens everyday.<br /> <br /> In our real world, people believe they have healing abilities.<br /> <br /> In a world of darkness where the tradition winned, it would be reality. What illness would exist when any ten person have &quot;the gift&quot; and can heal all issues? </div> </div> </div>I would argue that believing in a magical reality it's leagues different from believing that everyone has magic, simply because there's no reason to teach that any ten person have &quot;the gift&quot;. In our real world people believe SOME people have healing abilities. SOME special people get milacres. SOME very special people can heal. And this isn't new, in the middle ages people believed the same. Believing that magic exists in no way makes magic common.<br /> <br /> In Real Life many mystic traditions warded their lore for centuries. In Buddhism servants were killed if they heard the name of forbidden Buddhas by pouring molten iron in their ears. Hermetics and Gnostics had secret societies that would kill you if you betrayed them. Druids and other Pagans held secret enclaves with secret languages. And I could go on.<br /> <br /> Most Traditions are based one these people<br /> <br /> So, to be honest, no, I don't see the Old Traditions wanting a world where everyone believes that they have the spark of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And let's be honest Aleph, the whole &quot;the tradition never tried to disseminate it's tools in the consensus&quot; is just a narrative excuse to explain why the setting is the modern day world and not a high fantasy setting.<br /> <br /> Just like the revised edition &quot;traditions influence in the masses is more spiritual growth&quot; is just an excuse to avoid seeing a major shift in the world that would lead to mass numbers of sorcerers, and the end of mage's main narrative.<br /> <br /> That's the same reason why the Garou will always fail to gain significant victory over the Wyrm, it would break the game narrative. </div> </div> </div>No, what you're mentioning are the most basic premises of the Setting. It's a fundamental aspect of their Story.<br /> <br /> Garou always fail to gain significant victory over the Wyrm because they're bad at their job, that's what makes Werewolf a game about that dangers of Rage and a terrible past.<br /> <br /> Tradition mages only very recently started to care about the masses (and still have problems with this) because they're arrogant. That's what constitutes the theme of Hubris whitin Mage and informs the tragedy of the Traditions: They had a chance to make things right and defeat the Technocracy but they were too worried infigthing to take it. Would they change the tides now?...well, that's for your players to decide.<br /> <br /> What you call &quot;narrative excuses&quot; it's the heart of being part of a story of people that made mistakes and have to attone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take homeopathy and the lot of &quot;alternative medicine&quot;.<br /> <br /> Their mass popularity in the WOD is a good thing, after all, if anyone believe you can cure cancer with essential oil, it will become so.<br /> <br /> In fact, it should already be so with the common belief in it.<br /> <br /> As Phil Brucado explain in the M20 book of secrets, most people believe in magic, in a form and another, and believe they can do it, be it through prayer of seeing the local medicine man or joining a wicca circle.<br /> <br /> If the modern wod is anything like the real life modern world, then the traditions have won. And the consensus would have shifted to match this new reality. </div> </div> </div>It's not enough with believing in magic &quot;in a form and another&quot;. You need people to agree in what works and what doesn't, and to actively practice the magic, in order to alter the Consensus. Believing in Buddhism does nothing for a Christian, and believing in Evangelism won't always help Catholics (that would pray to saints).<br /> <br /> More so, Christians believe in God, but some don't believe in milacres. On the other hand even the most faithfull christians, if they have to chose between taking the bus to go to the Church and praying so an angel takes them there....they take the bus.<br /> <br /> Among other things because they believe in angels but not in that they're important enough to receive such service: See how the restrictive and elitist Paradigm of the Traditions impairs it's acceptance?. You need to Have (lot's and lot's of) Faith to, perhaps, get a milacre if God wants...but you don't need much to take a bus, and thus everyone uses buses. And that's what the Consensus needs, Magic it's instrumetal, people have to believe something works (regardless of how) to use it as magic.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy failed in making people dis-believe in the supernatural they have very much succeeded on making them believe Technology Works and it's there for you. Technology it's accepted by nearly everyone in the world, everywhere, even by those that don't believe in science!. While the different types of magic are much less universal<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The order of hermes is all for the development of humanity, the only difference with the order of reason was that the hermetic though the first thing to do was to understand magick before using it. </div> </div> </div>Which takes years of GRUELING Study and Practice worse than getting a Doctorate in hard sciences: Most people can't benefit from this. Most poeple aren't elite enough to survive Hermetic training and start using magic.<br /> <br /> Imagine a world where only scientists were able to use technology...<br /> <br /> For good or ill, Technocrats base their method on the idea that you don't need to understand science to be worthy of using it. That's not a minor difference, for the reasons I mentioned above. One could argue this difference is the reason Technocracy won the war - their milacres were a lot more accesible.<br /> <br /> Now, modern Hermetics have changed a lot. They still want people to go trough the whole process but they've chosen to publish their secret knowledge (well, adulterated versions of it). And that says something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know the ars magica is no longuer related to the wod, but it develop quite well early industrialition with the help of hermetic magic. </div> </div> </div>As Dataweaver said, in WoD it's different. WoD Hermetics haven't the same mentality. It's wrong to take Hermetics from other universe and say: See WoD Hermetics would have done the same!. If anything, those Hermetics are our Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-28-2018, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T12:37:59-08:00","id":1271539,"title":"","content":"One of the bigger influences on how I came to view and present the Void Engineers came from a Philip K. Dick story &quot;Souvenir&quot;, a synopsis and review of which can be found <a href=\"https://philipkdickreview.wordpress.com/2014/05/12/souvenir/\" target=\"_blank\">HERE</a>. In my games, they have been, since the 1920s (deliberately coinciding with HP Lovecraft's writing career), increasingly paranoid about what exists beyond the Gauntlet, and are devoted to keeping Earth and humanity safe and sanitized from &quot;alien&quot; influence. They're effectively Ghostbusters and Men in Black without the humor, in a world where things like The Astronaut's Wife, Stephen King's &quot;I am the Doorway&quot;, Lovecraft's &quot;The Whisperer in Darkness&quot; and John Carpenter's The Thing are all too real. They are the truth behind the stories of Majestic 12, Area 51, and Project Serpo. Weak points in the Gauntlet must be shorn up; People under the influence of extra dimensional beings must be rounded up and deprogramed; Non-human entities must be captured, studied and then eliminated. While some vestiges of 19th century ideas of exploitation of the beyond still remain, Sanitation is the goal, and any effort at exploration is only to further that end. <br /> <br /> And yes, I realize this is in stark contrast to the way most people have always viewed the Void Engineers. But it works for the sort of Mage games I usually prefer to run. Except for the times I feel like running Aliens space marines/Stargate/Star Trek mash ups. Then they are heroic explorers with lasers and space ships and ItX androids assistants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:38:52-08:00","id":1271588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271479#post1271479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The Technocracy believes that the consensus DOES control reality. The Void engineers patrol the umbra because their goal is to expand reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: this only works for a definition of \u201creality\u201d that largely excludes the Umbra. Which, to be fair, <i>does</i> match up with much of the Technocracy's worldview: see Tychoidean Cosmology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271479#post1271479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, no, the consensus doesn't work like that. Unconscious belief only has so much force behind it. If you split belief between modern medicine and Homeopathy, you don't get equally viable magical medicine and modern medicine that can cure everything. You get weaker and weaker versions of both. This is why the progenitors will kill you for being a faith healer even in othertimes cold conflict zones. Because you're weakening modern medicine with every convert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, I'm not so sure. I can definitely see this being the Technocracy's perspective, and the justification for insisting that everyone must buy into their worldview. But with the founding of the Traditions, the Order of Hermes and Ahl-i-Batin hit upon an alternate metaphysical framework (expressed in Book of Secrets as the \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d Paradigm) that <i>can</i> accommodate drastically different styles of magic without weakening each one. This is what sets them apart from the Disparates. <br /> <br /> That's the theory, at least. In practice, WAAGID is a Paradigm that's more suited to the Awakened than it is to Sleepers. Its main selling points are that the Awakened can more easily cooperate with each other and that Sleepers are more likely to Awaken when such a Paradigm is dominant. It's not completely devoid of benefit for Sleepers; but it also hasn't proven as effective at empowering Sleepers as technology has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:08:09-08:00","id":1271610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271588#post1271588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: this only works for a definition of \u201creality\u201d that largely excludes the Umbra. Which, to be fair, <i>does</i> match up with much of the Technocracy's worldview: see Tychoidean Cosmology.<br /> <br /> Here, I'm not so sure. I can definitely see this being the Technocracy's perspective, and the justification for insisting that everyone must buy into their worldview. But with the founding of the Traditions, the Order of Hermes and Ahl-i-Batin hit upon an alternate metaphysical framework (expressed in Book of Secrets as the \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d Paradigm) that <i>can</i> accommodate drastically different styles of magic without weakening each one. This is what sets them apart from the Disparates.<br /> <br /> That's the theory, at least. In practice, WAAGID is a Paradigm that's more suited to the Awakened than it is to Sleepers. Its main selling points are that the Awakened can more easily cooperate with each other and that Sleepers are more likely to Awaken when such a Paradigm is dominant. It's not completely devoid of benefit for Sleepers; but it also hasn't proven as effective at empowering Sleepers as technology has.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Fair point. The perspective I posted is however, more than likely how the Union sees things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:47:31-08:00","id":1271615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot#post1268969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run Mage chronicles but enjoy reading about the other lines. Beckett's Jyhad Diary was a giant update of everything in Vampire that happened between 2004 and 2014 or so and is 500 gorgeous pages of notes, pictures, and such. I very much wish there were a Mage analog.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one that wished M20 had a metaplot update? The Metaplot asides gave options but didn't include much detail on &quot;hey, this is what a world where the avatar storm died down would look like&quot; or &quot;hey, here are some masters that could return to the other side of the gauntlet&quot;. I tend to get plots from picking elements from the metaplot and using those to create large arcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrary to how the forums tend to go, regarding metaplot, I agree with this OP. I liked M20's &quot;New Millenium&quot; metaplot direction and I'd like to see more of it.<br /> <br /> Generally, I get why a certain demographics of people tend to not like metaplot and why those tend to be the most active people on forums and such. However, I do like metaplot and tend to gravitate toward settings whichhave some measure of it. I like to follow the story from book-to-book, I like having characters to relate to. I like to see how the setting looks from the viewpoint of those characters &quot;on the ground&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yes, sometimes, i hate when the metaplot goes in a direction I'm against (see V5), but all-in-all, I'd rather have metaplot, than not.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I do wish M20 having a metaplot update. The basis was good, I'd like to see it expanding. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T20:23:36-08:00","id":1271675,"title":"","content":"I like Metaplot, it makes for all kinds of fun things to play with or twist or whatever.<br /> <br /> M20's Metaplot was terrible. But then, 90% of M20 was terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T21:38:41-08:00","id":1271685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271615#post1271615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, I do wish M20 having a metaplot update.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dante's Ascension Blog?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T02:36:39-08:00","id":1271725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271685#post1271685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dante's Ascension Blog?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall reading a Mage game online set in a contemporary setting in which one of the new things that had happened was that the Virtual Adepts had set up a wiki which also doubled as a social network that all the Traditions used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T09:10:52-08:00","id":1271781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271685#post1271685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dante's Ascension Blog?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last entry in it being &quot;Screw you guys, I'm ascending.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T10:07:13-08:00","id":1271793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1271781#post1271781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last entry in it being &quot;Screw you guys, I'm ascending.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I'm not certain Dante would be that rude, but otherwise a fitting ending.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:56:32-08:00","id":1271969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<br /> As Enginseer-42 says, they believe that Consensus controls Reality. Technocrats don't believe Umbrood are outside the influence of the Consensus, but the Consensus isn't <i>wise</i> - the Consensus needs to be controled. That's what Technocrats do. They believe their efforts strengthen the Gauntlet and help making these incursions from Spirits a non threat. If spirits, even good intended ones, were allowed to interact with humans, human belief would weaken the Gauntlet and then evil spirits would have an easier time entering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course they can be a resource, but what I intended to higlight was that they're not <i>essential </i>to the long term plans of the Technocracy as far as they understand Reality.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, the Technocracy don't believe that the consensus controls reality, not counting that they believe in objective Natural Constants (tm) without which they would be nothing else than reality deviants, and that would be preposterous right?<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Tichoidian model on which they depend to explain the umbra and the consensus doesn't place the consensus as the ultimate mover of the cosmos. For Tichoidians, the universe created umbra for beaten realities long before humanity bursted in.<br /> <br /> In fact, for VE, it isn't much a matter of gauntlet rather than a metric of information possessed by the entity trying to enter. <br /> <br /> The idea that there is an objective gauntlet metric, separating equally all umbrood from humanity is purely out of character rules. For the VE, entities's ability to goes to earth depend on how much they &quot;match&quot; as an individual the expectations of the consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quote<br /> &quot;if spiritis, even good intended ones, were allowed to interact with humans, human belief would weaken the Gauntlet and then evil spirits would have an easier time entering&quot;. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not an all or nothing situation.<br /> Let's give an exemple.<br /> <br /> The technocracy pass words than an Obedient Benevolent Species (let's call it OBS) existing on a planet outside of ours is coming to seek a new master race after their creator disappeared and want to serve US. What a chance!<br /> <br /> Now, the VE would have no problem seeking in the high umbra a spirit brood based on the archetype of the Devoted and Benevolent Servant. By transmitting the belief in the extraterestrial servants coming from space and coming to YOU, from &quot;specialised decontamination centers&quot;, the technocracy technically allows theses archetypal servants to pass the gauntlet and materialise in the centers, which are nothing but technocratic holds.<br /> <br /> So only a specific kind of benevolent species enter, after all, this unique species is believed to be benevolent, how a malevolent one could match the expectation of the public and pass the gauntlet?<br /> <br /> Fun fact, polls shows that despite the tone of our extraterrestrial invasions pop culture, we as a people, are greatly open to the arrival of aliens on earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> &quot;[The thing that stops Technocrats from doing the same it's that human agents are easy to come by and are dupes that don't know who they're working for. Necronauts are rare, and Wraiths have a Shadow (aren't trustworthy) and are very aware of the supernatural (aren't dupes). There's no way for the Techncoracy to treat a Necropolis the same way they treat a normal city. Especially not with the little understanding they have on the Dark Umbra and it's politics (which it's hard to overcme because necronauts are rare).<br /> &quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Necronauts are rare only becauve the VE cutted the program after the great malstrom. And wraith can be conditionned. Dimensional science + Mind allow to influence the mind of a spirit. In fact, that would allow the technocracy an extremely uselfy bait.<br /> <br /> &quot;Serves these guys agaisnt the Empires that you never liked in the first place, and they'll make your shadow finally shut up!<br /> <br /> As for the politics, all wraiths begin with no understanding about the dark umbra and the way it's societies works, that's no excuse, if an individual wraith can learn it quickly enough to defend herself agaisnt the hasards of stygian politics, the VE have no excuse.<br /> <br /> They had necronauts (mostly) safe in the labyrinth. After that, it's impossible to say that they couldn't have influence in the dark kingdoms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot; would argue that believing in a magical reality it's leagues different from believing that everyone has magic&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> And I would answer that all culture believing in magic all believed as well that everybody had some influence or magic of himself.<br /> <br /> From the idea that anyone can pray to the almighty in monotheistic religions or that alien technology is usable by anyone in modern UFO new age beliefs.<br /> <br /> In fact, I would like to know if you have an exemple of a spcific belief in magic in the real world that exclude all but an elite from the power of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quote &quot;simply because there's no reason to teach that any ten person have &quot;the gift&quot;&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> If you speak of the traditions, then, they have such reasons, doing so would allow any little community to have a healer to heal anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> In our real world people believe SOME people have healing abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because in our real world, this isn't true.<br /> <br /> In the WOD, in a community believe in healers, they would objectively heal people.<br /> <br /> Think of the New age communities that believes that anyone have intrinsect control over one's own health.<br /> In a world where reality is defined by beliefs, those would be facts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Most Traditions are based one these people<br /> <br /> So, to be honest, no, I don't see the Old Traditions wanting a world where everyone believes that they have the spark of magic.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Think less on the real world inspiration and more on what the BOOKS says.<br /> <br /> And the books are clear: the traditions fight for a world where ultimately, there wouldn't be any sleepers anymore, but an enlightened humanity. In a world of magic.<br /> <br /> And it's been that since the first edition books.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while The OOH want to be a guiding hand, they desire a world of Awakened, not serfs.<br /> <br /> As for your exemples of real life magical societies, remember that in the WOD, theses people can't do that, because magic is no objective formulation that you can keep for yourself by killing people.<br /> <br /> In The WOD, if the traditions wins and shows that magic exist, it's not them that'll decide what it'll look like (the technocracy itself have a hard time making people accept specific rules for a fixed system, so &quot;magic&quot;...).<br /> <br /> If after the revelation, Europeans believes that magic is like harry potter movies where people with a gift can cast spells with a wand and pseudo latin, Japanese believes it's a mish mash of pop culture magical system and japanese tradition, etc...<br /> <br /> That's how it will be, no matter how much the traditions would protest.<br /> <br /> After all, they do accept that all are free to follow their own paradigms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;No, what you're mentioning are the most basic premises of the Setting. It's a fundamental aspect of their Story. </div> </div> </div>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I won't mention that the setting was majorly retconned after first edition, or the whole idea of paradigm will have to go out of the fundamental aspects of the story.<br /> <br /> But the consensus of Apathy isn't a premise of the Setting, neither is the idea that all efforts of the traditions only help with spiritual growth.<br /> <br /> Remember that the point of the Order of hermes and the sons of ether was to infiltrate academics and science to subvert the technocratic paradigm up to the very science they promote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<br /> It's not enough with believing in magic &quot;in a form and another&quot;. You need people to agree in what works and what doesn't, and to actively practice the magic, in order to alter the Consensus. Believing in Buddhism does nothing for a Christian, and believing in Evangelism won't always help Catholics (that would pray to saints).<br /> <br /> More so, Christians believe in God, but some don't believe in milacres. On the other hand even the most faithfull christians, if they have to chose between taking the bus to go to the Church and praying so an angel takes them there....they take the bus.<br /> <br /> Among other things because they believe in angels but not in that they're important enough to receive such service: See how the restrictive and elitist Paradigm of the Traditions impairs it's acceptance?. You need to Have (lot's and lot's of) Faith to, perhaps, get a milacre if God wants...but you don't need much to take a bus, and thus everyone uses buses. And that's what the Consensus needs, Magic it's instrumetal, people have to believe something works (regardless of how) to use it as magic.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy failed in making people dis-believe in the supernatural they have very much succeeded on making them believe Technology Works and it's there for you. Technology it's accepted by nearly everyone in the world, everywhere, even by those that don't believe in science!. While the different types of magic are much less universal&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> None of that is necessary. First, reality zones are a thing, and were since the introduction of the Taftani.<br /> <br /> Second, have you read Dark ages Mage?<br /> <br /> You don't need the whole population to agree on the One True Way of Magic, just to make them accept magic.<br /> <br /> After that, every community will be based on it's own beliefs of what magic is, faith healers will probably explode in numbers in italia and usa, fantasy fans will have disparate ways, etc...<br /> Their beliefs will collide with what they see works on the other side of the world and evolve without a specific direction.<br /> <br /> Just as the council wants.<br /> <br /> As for your exemple of the faithful that must choose between a bus and praying to an angel.<br /> <br /> First, as perpetually repeated in the books of revised edition, it's not technology or magic, both can exist side by side.<br /> <br /> And second, the reason why faithful people don't call angels to carry them to church in the real world may be because that doesn't work, just saying.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: there's a group described in guide to the traditions that call an angel named Sophia to talk to the radio. They have assembled a massive community, so much that verbena and dreamspeaker think of doing the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Which takes years of GRUELING Study and Practice worse than getting a Doctorate in hard sciences: Most people can't benefit from this. Most poeple aren't elite enough to survive Hermetic training and start using magic.<br /> <br /> Imagine a world where only scientists were able to use technology...&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> You forget sorcerers, you forget wonders.<br /> <br /> You're literally using all the arguments in the convention books revised, which is made from the extremely narrow pov of technocrats. if you want to know what may actually happens if mystics have their ways, throw away the opinion of the technocracts and open the tradition books and the guide to the tradition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or look into the book of mirrors, there is an alternate setting where the traditions won in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As Dataweaver said, in WoD it's different. WoD Hermetics haven't the same mentality. It's wrong to take Hermetics from other universe and say: See WoD Hermetics would have done the same!. If anything, those Hermetics are our Technocrats.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> It's also wrong to take the real life Hermetics, people believing they knew objective laws of magics and behave accordingly to say anything about the behavior of the hermetics of a world where magick take as many form as imagination allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T18:00:28-08:00","id":1272089,"title":"","content":"No. The Technocracy VERY MUCH SO believes that the Consensus controls reality. Their entire organization is based upon that assumption.<br /> <br /> The books are clear. The Traditions SAY they're fighting for magic for everyone, but they're still the same hidebound jerks they were in the middle ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T19:08:13-08:00","id":1272100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1272089#post1272089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The Technocracy VERY MUCH SO believes that the Consensus controls reality. Their entire organization is based upon that assumption.<br /> <br /> The books are clear. The Traditions SAY they're fighting for magic for everyone, but they're still the same hidebound jerks they were in the middle ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to disagree on both counts, sort of.<br /> <br /> First, the Technocracy definitely believes that the Masses <i>influence</i> Reality; but they also acknowledge that there's an underlying Truth that you can either work with our work against (the so-called Earthly Foundations). And they pride themselves with working with it: they see Enlightened Science as an extension of the natural order \u2014 what Reality would be like without mage interference. Their claim is that this is why they've been so successful in getting their ideas accepted by the Masses; and it's this notion that they're building on a foundation of absolute truths which they use to justify what they're doing as Science. <br /> <br /> And no, the Traditions are <i>not</i> the same hidebound jerks they were in the middle ages; they're post-modern progressive jerks. This is what distinguishes them from the Disparates, who by and large are still largely stuck in the past, attempting to hold onto their glory days. At the heart of the Traditions is a shared metaphysics that's flexible enough to be consistent with a broad range of magical practices \u2014 what earlier editions called the Metaphysics of Magick, and what M20 calls the \u201cWe Are All Gods In Disguise\u201d Paradigm. It gives them a shared mindset that facilitates cooperation and an overall goal that unites them \u2014 thus, \u201cpost-modern and progressive\u201d. But make no mistake: they're still arrogant jerks who see mages as being better than Sleepers; and their overall plan to help the Sleepers generally boils down to some form of \u201chelp all of them to Awaken\u201d. Indeed, there are even some who are concerned that efforts to make life more bearable for Sleepers is a Bad Thing, because it discourages them from Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T19:59:07-08:00","id":1272105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1272100#post1272100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll have to disagree on both counts, sort of.<br /> <br /> First, the Technocracy definitely believes that the Masses <i>influence</i> Reality; but they also acknowledge that there's an underlying Truth that you can either work with our work against (the so-called Earthly Foundations). And they pride themselves with working with it: they see Enlightened Science as an extension of the natural order \u2014 what Reality would be like without mage interference. Their claim is that this is why they've been so successful in getting their ideas accepted by the Masses; and it's this notion that they're building on a foundation of absolute truths which they use to justify what they're doing as Science.<br /> <br /> And no, the Traditions are <i>not</i> the same hidebound jerks they were in the middle ages; they're post-modern progressive jerks. This is what distinguishes them from the Disparates, who by and large are still largely stuck in the past, attempting to hold onto their glory days. At the heart of the Traditions is a shared metaphysics that's flexible enough to be consistent with a broad range of magical practices \u2014 what earlier editions called the Metaphysics of Magick, and what M20 calls the \u201cWe Are All Gods In Disguise\u201d Paradigm. It gives them a shared mindset that facilitates cooperation and an overall goal that unites them \u2014 thus, \u201cpost-modern and progressive\u201d. But make no mistake: they're still arrogant jerks who see mages as being better than Sleepers; and their overall plan to help the Sleepers generally boils down to some form of \u201chelp all of them to Awaken\u201d. Indeed, there are even some who are concerned that efforts to make life more bearable for Sleepers is a Bad Thing, because it discourages them from Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps in M20 that's how the Technocracy works, but I've made my opinions on M20's lore clear.<br /> <br /> Fair point on the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T20:39:40-08:00","id":1272110,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I have a rather low opinion of pre-M20 lore where the Technocracy is concerned; all too often, it boils down to \u201cthe higher-ups in the Union are liars, and the rest of them are dupes\u201d. In the decade between the end of the classical World of Darkness and its rebirth with the Revised Convention Books and then M20, I worked up a head-canon to explain how the Union's perspective could be handled in a way that allows them to actually make valid points, and not just be liars and dupes. It just so happens that the bulk of the M20 lore pertaining to the Union is fully consistent with said head-canon. (I'm not fond of the Technephandi stuff, as I prefer the Union's flaws to be their own rather than the result of infiltration; but other than that, I prefer it to the earlier editions' fundamentally flawed approach.)<br /> <br /> As such, and since this is a thread about M5 Metaplot (that is, \u201cwhat happens next?\u201d), I'm inclined to take the M20 lore as a starting point and go from there.<br /> <br /> And for the record, the Union has always, in all editions, held that their Science is based on fundamental truths about the nature of Reality. In the First and Second Editions, this flew in the face of the argument that Reality is Subjective, which was the biggest cause of the aforementioned \u201cthey're either liars or dupes\u201d issue. Revised introduced such notions as Cosmological Constants and Historical Inertia, which are what I originally based my head-canon for a less stupid Union on, in that they're examples of how Reality <i>isn't</i> exclusively a product of the Consensus. What M20 brings to the picture are the Reality Zones, and a mention when discussing the Technocratic Zones that the Union believes that their Zones are closer to the \u201cbase reality\u201d than other Zones are. It's a shift from the earliest Edition's portrayal of Technocrats as \u201cMagick isn't real, and I'll shoot you if you say or do otherwise\u201d to a more nuanced view where the Union views Enlightened Science as the best option possible, to the point where they're willing to push it on everyone \u201cfor their own good\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-01-2018, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T09:48:03-08:00","id":1272404,"title":"","content":"A bit torn on the question of metaplot. On one hand i like the extra flavor and feeling that there is areal living world going on around you that you get from metaplot. And i like much of the direction of the metaplot in M20. But i also find it can get very complicated and honestly rather pretentious at times. But after years of running Awakening precisely because I was tired of the metaplot I realize i kind of miss at least some of the deeper plot and background from Ascension. Oy, the dllemma! In particular i find that metaplot tends to engage one the things I like least in rpg players which is the tendency to take metaplot and background in the game literature as absolute and unchangeable. Truth is i have never played Mage (either version) as written straight out of the box. So the more metaplot, the more I fear players will be annoying about whether I include it or not. That ultimately is why I liked the M20 approach of providing metaplot in a modular way. If you want to take the metaplot,great. if not, also great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T08:03:41-08:00","id":1272844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270886#post1270886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy actually has a Mission statement and its not &quot;Exploring and investigating reality&quot;<br /> (...)<br /> Its right there.. its in the guide to the Technocracy, its in mage 20.. there's no place where the Technocracy is guided by &quot;Explore and investigate reality&quot; vs &quot;Create orderly Utopia&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1270892#post1270892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, the idea of knowledge it's always subordinate to the idea of defining an orderly reality with the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am getting 'investigating and exploring reality' as a major goal of the Technocracy from the first and, maybe, fourth points of the Precepts of Damian ( These parts : &quot;Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be won.&quot; and &quot;Knowledge must be absolute or chaos will envelop all&quot; . ) . I didn't mean to say that this is the main or the only goal of the Technocracy. I don't think the Technocracy has a single, defined goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T16:47:39-08:00","id":1272907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1269566#post1269566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am hoping for the &quot;buffett&quot; approach Dogstar mentions, in that the book presents a number of opportunities. That would make it a more flexible tool for gamers, while a book with only one story is limited and too proscriptive. Maybe the Technocracy is riddled with a metastisized Nephandi threat, and maybe the Technos purged the Fallen, but both options should easily be available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocracy Reloaded is going to be metaplot-agnostic IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T11:26:20-08:00","id":1272995,"title":"","content":"It might be. They might reserve the Metaplot advancement for M5, which I do expect will be more along the lines of Brucato's \u201cMage: the New Millennium\u201d (restructuring the Council of Nine and renaming many of the Traditions; reorganizing the Union and instituting a Purge; and bringing the Disparate Alliance or of the shadows). But at the least, I expect that the outlines for New Millennium plot advancements will be included in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T14:50:33-08:00","id":1273016,"title":"","content":"I don't like the Purge as a concept - it seems designed to try and reset the clock to 1e when it was white hats vs black hats. Now using an attempted purge of idealists/reformers (by technephandi/Threat Null/Technocrat hardliners) to trigger a Technocratic Civil War in the style of the second scenario in <i>Ascension ... </i>that's a more interesting concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T16:25:31-08:00","id":1273024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273016#post1273016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the Purge as a concept - it seems designed to try and reset the clock to 1e when it was white hats vs black hats. Now using an attempted purge of idealists/reformers (by technephandi/Threat Null/Technocrat hardliners) to trigger a Technocratic Civil War in the style of the second scenario in <i>Ascension ... </i>that's a more interesting concept.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Looks at V5 in comparison to v1*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T21:48:53-08:00","id":1273051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273024#post1273024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks at V5 in comparison to v1*</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting, and astute, observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T22:38:10-08:00","id":1273058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273016#post1273016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the Purge as a concept - it seems designed to try and reset the clock to 1e when it was white hats vs black hats. Now using an attempted purge of idealists/reformers (by technephandi/Threat Null/Technocrat hardliners) to trigger a Technocratic Civil War in the style of the second scenario in <i>Ascension ... </i>that's a more interesting concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that the upcoming \u201cpurge\u201d is actually going to end up as a Technocratic Civil War of sorts: it appears that Navalon will be the idealists/reformers that survive the purge. They'll still be Technocrats; but aside from some moles in the Union, they'll no longer be part of the Union. My own wishful thinking is that they'll retain enough power and influence that you can play them like the Technocracy of the Revised Convention Books (the so-called \u201ckinder and gentler\u201d Technocracy that isn't beholden to Control) while leaving the Reloaded Technocracy more ruthless and under Control's thumb than ever before. <br /> <br /> As for Threat Null: my personal take on it is that Threat Null, not the Nephandi, is behind the infiltration of the Union and will instigate the purge; it's in keeping with the nature of the Schism being between out-of-touch management who dwell on the elegance of their models on the one hand, and the down-to-Earth field agents who have to witness first-hand what happens when they attempt to put those models into practice. As well, I prefer the Union's problems be homegrown, not the result of outside manipulation. As long as the Metaplot is such that it allows for this possibility, I'll be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T06:20:23-08:00","id":1273085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273058#post1273058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Threat Null: my personal take on it is that Threat Null, not the Nephandi, is behind the infiltration of the Union and will instigate the purge; it's in keeping with the nature of the Schism being between out-of-touch management who dwell on the elegance of their models on the one hand, and the down-to-Earth field agents who have to witness first-hand what happens when they attempt to put those models into practice. As well, I prefer the Union's problems be homegrown, not the result of outside manipulation. As long as the Metaplot is such that it allows for this possibility, I'll be happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, there's nothing wrong with Nephandi being more prevalent than before, but Threat Null it's too good an antagonist to loose.<br /> <br /> 1ed Mage focused on the protags being the &quot;balance&quot; between the Triad of Dynamism(Marauders), Entropy(Nephandi), and Stasis(the Technocracy). But the Technocracy become more humane to be playable and gathered a huge number of fans (and, really, the hippism of &quot;standard technology is Banal&quot; doesn't hold out for an adult 21th century audience), and thus the inhumane Threat Null becomes a much more fitting antagonist to take the seat of Statism.<br /> <br /> Threat Null being in charge of part of a Pogrom-friendly Technocracy can easily mirror the fear of AI taking control of the world (with the Autochtonians, who probably serve the Computer), while also keeping the dilema of Security vs Freedom (supernaturals ARE dangerous) and the critique against excesive state-surveilance (That, in my opinion, it's still current. Think Assange case, or the more recent Facebook scandal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T07:41:01-08:00","id":1273096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273058#post1273058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that the upcoming \u201cpurge\u201d is actually going to end up as a Technocratic Civil War of sorts: it appears that Navalon will be the idealists/reformers that survive the purge. They'll still be Technocrats; but aside from some moles in the Union, they'll no longer be part of the Union. My own wishful thinking is that they'll retain enough power and influence that you can play them like the Technocracy of the Revised Convention Books (the so-called \u201ckinder and gentler\u201d Technocracy that isn't beholden to Control) while leaving the Reloaded Technocracy more ruthless and under Control's thumb than ever before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far better and more sensible than having them join the Disparate Alliance. They'd essentially be fighting to save the Union from itself ... which is far thematically richer for a Technocracy chronicle than Technos vs. Trads.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> How I would set up the factions in M5:<br /> <br /> THE TRADITIONS<br /> -Seek to keep magic and mysticism alive in the modern world, generally fine with modern society and technology.<br /> -Order of Hermes,<br /> -Euthanatos/Chakravanti<br /> -Solificati/Children of Knowledge<br /> -Ahl-i-Batin<br /> -Verbena<br /> -Dreamspeakers/Kha'vadi<br /> -Celestial Chorus<br /> -Akashayana<br /> -CoX/Sahajiya<br /> <br /> THE NEW ORDER OF REASON<br /> -Seek to purge the corrupted leaders of the Technocracy to establish a safe, stable reality and lead mankind into a technological utopia.<br /> -IBM (International Brotherhood of Mechanicians), ItX as presented in Revised<br /> -Virtual Adepts<br /> -Society of Ether (Highly tense with the others apart from the Adepts, it's unclear if they'll stick on after Threat Null is dealt with)<br /> -Revised Syndicate<br /> -Revised Progenitors (One of the smallest conventions of the NOR, large numbers stayed with the Technocracy)<br /> -Lightkeepers (Revised NWO, also rather small)<br /> -Void Engineers<br /> <br /> TECHNOCRATIC UNION<br /> -Corrupted by Threat Null, the leadership have become as ruthless and totalitarian as they were back in the early 90s. These co-opted elements must be taken down before they break down the Gauntlet and allow Threat Null to openly invade Earth ...<br /> <br /> ROGUE COUNCIL<br /> -Fanatical traditionalists led by spiritised Tradition archmasters in the Umbra. The strawman version of the Traditions, these are radicals who reject the New Horizon Council and want to bring modern civilisation down so they can party like it's 1399.<br /> <br /> NEPHANDI AND MARAUDERS<br /> -You know the drill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 12-06-2018, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T10:43:48-08:00","id":1273113,"title":"","content":"1. I'd have the Dreamspeakers switch their name to the Kha'vadi; and it's a given that the other New Council renamings (Akashic Brotherhood to Akashayana, Cult of Ecstasy to Sahajiya, Euthanatos to Chakravanti, Sons of Ether to Society of Ether, even Virtual Adepts to Mercurial Elite) would take effect.<br /> <br /> 2. With those last two, I'd keep them on the New Council, especially the Society of Ether. But they'd be the most friendly toward the new Order of Reason, and many of these two Traditions might \u201cdefect\u201d to the Order. There wouldn't be enough of them to form new Conventions; most of the VA \u201cdefectors\u201d would land in the IBM, and the former Etherites would end up all over the place (with the more kooky ones forming a new Special Projects Division within the Syndicate that has nothing to do with Pentex or the Wyrm and everything to do with <i>Fringe</i>). <br /> <br /> 3. Threat Null would indeed be behind the \u201creformation\u201d of the Union. But they wouldn't be <i>preparing for</i> an invasion of the Earth; their takeover of the Union would <i>be</i> their \u201cinvasion\u201d. <br /> <br /> 4. A new kind of Marauder, the Negation Men (first introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b>) would arise, embodying Denial in the same way that more traditional Marauders embody Madness. Unlike how they're presented in <b>Book of Secrets</b>, they don't reject <i>all</i> magick, per se; each has his own Focus, just like any other mage, and stuff that would be Coincidental in a Reality Zone dominated by his Focus works fine for him. This makes it even harder to identify them than depicted in <b>Book of Secrets</b>; and they're frequently found within other factions, with the single largest infestation being within the Technocratic Union: use Technocratic Negation Men to represent those 1e- and 2e-style Technocrats who actually <i>don't</i> believe in mysticism and are all for Stasis \u2014 but they've weaponized their Denial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T11:55:37-08:00","id":1273125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273113#post1273113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. With those last two, I'd keep them on the New Council, especially the Society of Ether. But they'd be the most friendly toward the new Order of Reason, and many of these two Traditions might \u201cdefect\u201d to the Order. There wouldn't be enough of them to form new Conventions; most of the VA \u201cdefectors\u201d would land in the IBM, and the former Etherites would end up all over the place (with the more kooky ones forming a new Special Projects Division within the Syndicate that has nothing to do with Pentex or the Wyrm and everything to do with <i>Fringe</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that might be a better way to play it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Threat Null would indeed be behind the \u201creformation\u201d of the Union. But they wouldn't be <i>preparing for</i> an invasion of the Earth; their takeover of the Union would <i>be</i> their \u201cinvasion\u201d. </div> </div> </div>I can view it as the opening stages of the &quot;invasion&quot;, with the bulk of them (particularly the Autopolitans and Transhumans) still being held off in the Umbra by Paradox and the Void Engineers. But Agents and Residents would be present on Earth in various amounts, as they can actually survive on Earth for extended periods of time (and pass for human ... somewhat).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T12:33:13-08:00","id":1273131,"title":"","content":"As for the Disparate Alliance: I <i>would</i> make them a thing, with their \u201ccoming out party\u201d coinciding with the Technocratic split. There exactly the sort of thing the Batini would come up with. But I'd make a point to show that it's not Traditions 2.0: the only thing holding them together is a mutual fear of the Technocracy and distrust of the Traditions. In particular, Is use them to illustrate by counterexample the common ground that unites the Traditions: they are what so many say the Traditions are; and by highlighting how they differ from the Traditions, you can more clearly see what the Traditions are like. <br /> <br /> Navalon/the new Order of Reason isn't part of the Disparate Alliance; but I can see them being grateful if the Alliance had a hand in the nascent Order of Reason surviving the Technocratic purge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T12:45:25-08:00","id":1273132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273131#post1273131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Disparate Alliance: I <i>would</i> make them a thing, with their \u201ccoming out party\u201d coinciding with the Technocratic split. There exactly the sort of thing the Batini would come up with. But I'd make a point to show that it's not Traditions 2.0: the only thing holding them together is a mutual fear of the Technocracy and distrust of the Traditions. In particular, Is use them to illustrate by counterexample the common ground that unites the Traditions: they are what so many say the Traditions are; and by highlighting how they differ from the Traditions, you can more clearly see what the Traditions are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think of my Rogue Council, BTW? They're intended to demonstrate what the Traditions are not from a different angle (as antagonists to all other factions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Navalon/the new Order of Reason isn't part of the Disparate Alliance; but I can see them being grateful if the Alliance had a hand in the nascent Order of Reason surviving the Technocratic purge. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the NOR would be more tolerant of non-Nephandi/Marauders/Rogue Council mage groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T13:04:23-08:00","id":1273134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1268969-am-i-the-only-one-who-wished-m20-had-more-metaplot?p=1273113#post1273113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I'd have the Dreamspeakers switch their name to the Kha'vadi; and it's a given that the other New Council renamings (Akashic Brotherhood to Akashayana, Cult of Ecstasy to Sahajiya, Euthanatos to Chakravanti, Sons of Ether to Society of Ether, even Virtual Adepts to Mercurial Elite) would take effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have all these renamings, all but one. ( I do think the Society of the Ether is needed for the obvious reason of making it gender-neutral. And it does sound good. )<br /> You can even have the nice sounding, but plain ' Mercurial Elite ' replacing the classic and 90s Virtual Adepts.<br /> But do let one remain - let the Cult of Ecstasy keep their current faction name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-09-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}